A||||8||BAM-BAM||What are they?||||4||
Z||000000||BAM-BAM||02-29-2000||09:26 PM||||   I have searched and searched for any kind of diagram or explanation that might enlighten me as to the purpose and function of the two pipes in the extreme rear of the engine compartment. One deadends just in back of the EGR on the left and the other curls under on the right. They both seem to pass through some kind of manifold in the trunk. Niether Seem to be going anywhere. WHAT ARE THEY? ||||reg||4
Z||000001||fiero56||02-29-2000||09:40 PM||||Cooling tubes leading from a fan. They blow cooler air on the coil and alternator.||||reg||1
Z||000002||BAM-BAM||02-29-2000||09:55 PM||||    Is there a particular nomencature for the tubes? How is the fan powered?||||reg||1
Z||000003||AL||02-29-2000||10:23 PM||||they are activated when your car gets hot and when you turn on the air conditioner, if it doesn't come on when you hit the air then you have a problem, AL.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Ed||03-01-2000||12:05 AM||||Peel back the trunk liner on the passenger side and you'll see the blower motor. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||DRH||03-01-2000||01:47 PM||||To elaborate on what Al said... The blower should come on anytime the radiator fan does.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Old Lar||03-01-2000||04:52 PM||||The pipes cool things that don't take kindly to heating, the coil, the alternator.  It gives you something to polish in the engine compartment.||||reg||1
Z||000007||SCCA FIERO||03-01-2000||06:55 PM||||When I put a V6 in my Coupe there were no holes to put those pipes and blower in. I hope nothing melts back there. I drove it all last summer in 95* weather so I guess it'll be okay.  :::crossing fingers:::||||reg||1
Z||000008||Robert||03-01-2000||07:29 PM||||My 87GT has them.  I think it was a brainstorm of GM, but they didn’t use them on the 88 models.  Therefore they must not be really needed.||||reg||3
